$vb(c) dot (vb(a) times vb(b))$ is a signed volume: it is positive when $vb(a), vb(b), vb(c)$ constitute a right-handed set, and zero iff the three vectors are coplanar, that is, one is a linear combination of the other two. In $RR^2$, the analogous bracket $[vb(a), vb(b)] = epsilon_(i j) a_i b_j = a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1$ gives the signed area of the parallelogram formed by $vb(a)$ and $vb(b)$.
